# 52. Research Success Criteria

Kitty × Tweak Labs succeeds when it produces:

- reproducible experiments
- genuine technical understanding
- useful open-source projects
- independent model implementations
- documented architectural discoveries
- credible benchmark results
- increasingly capable infrastructure
- educational material
- stable operating systems and tooling
- working distributed systems

Success is **not measured solely by model size**.

A clever 200M model experiment can matter more than an unexplained 7B checkpoint.

---

# 53. Long-Term Vision

The ultimate goal is to progressively transform:

```text
Two developers
        ↓
Two independent research ecosystems
        ↓
Shared experiments
        ↓
Shared tooling
        ↓
Distributed home lab
        ↓
Original models
        ↓
Original architectures
        ↓
Published research
        ↓
Professional research laboratory
```

Kitty × Tweak Labs may eventually support research across:

- artificial intelligence
- language models
- operating systems
- distributed systems
- cybersecurity
- developer tooling
- agents
- networking
- edge computing
- hardware acceleration

---

# 54. The Core Principle

The defining principle of Kitty × Tweak Labs should remain:

> **We do not need a datacenter before we can do real research.**

We need:

- questions worth answering
- experiments designed properly
- measurements we can trust
- systems we understand
- documentation others can reproduce
- and the willingness to keep learning.

The hardware can grow with the research.

The research comes first.

---

